    "rationale": "The Builder's proposal changes only sensor_size, from 0.016 to 0.012 m, relative to iteration 4 (58.54, the best so far). Iteration 4's controller is kept unchanged so the race isolates the footprint change. Iteration 8 (forward row moved to y=0.03) fell to 41.1, and iteration 2 (y=0.07, confounded with a lighter body) fell to 47.8, so the y=0.05 lead stays. Iteration 7 (wheel_radius 0.025) scored 57.9 and iteration 5 (0.04) scored 41.4, so radius 0.03 m stays. Iteration 6 (mass 1.0) scored 42.7, so mass 0.8 kg stays. Iteration 3 and 4 showed that wheel_track 0.08 m is the best measured track width, so it stays. The 12 mm footprint reads a sharper line position, but its reach is smaller: a sensor sees tape only within about 0.0185 m of its centre. The outer sensors at x=±0.06 therefore see the tape only for line offsets up to about ±0.0785 m, compared with ±0.082 m at 16 mm. Line loss is rare at iteration 4 (oval 0, s-bend 0.95, slalom 0.85), so this small loss of reach is the main risk. The controller is therefore unchanged: kp 1.35, ki 0.02, kd 0.25, weights proportional to x (clipped at ±2), base_speed 1.5 and last_direction recovery. Expected result, not measured: max_error and steering_oscillation at or slightly below iteration 4, progress at or above 0.185 on the s-bend, and a score near 58.",
