    "feedback": "Written before this candidate has raced, so it makes no claim about its result. Iteration 4 (16 mm, y=0.05, wheel_track 0.08, radius 0.03, mass 0.8, kp 1.35) is the best design at 58.54, and every run ends off_track with max_error on the 0.06 m floor. Iteration 8 showed that moving the sensors forward to y=0.03 cut the score to 41.1, and iteration 2 showed that y=0.07 (confounded with a lighter body) cut it to 47.8, so the y=0.05 lead is the best measured. Iterations 5, 6 and 7 showed that wheel_radius 0.04 (41.4), mass 1.0 (42.7) and wheel_radius 0.025 (57.9) all score at or below iteration 4, so those stay. Because the footprint is the only change, I kept the iteration 4 controller. A 12 mm footprint reaches only about ±0.0785 m at the outer sensors, compared with ±0.082 m at 16 mm, so line loss at the edges is the main risk. When the race reports: if s-bend progress holds at or above 0.185 with line_loss_events at or below iteration 4 (s-bend 0.95, slalom 0.85) and max_error falls, keep 12 mm and try the next request. If line loss rises at the edges, restore 16 mm.",
